        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Lands Moyessa, Listowel, Co. Kerry, \r\n\r\nc. 24.69ha - c. 61 acres\r\n\r\nFor Sale by Live Virtual Online & Public Auction\r\n\r\nWednesday 14th of October 2026. \r\n\r\nAt\r\n\r\nWilsons Auctions, Kingswood Interchange, Naas Road, Dublin 22\r\n\r\nExcellent Location \r\n\r\nLocation Listowel 3km, Abbeyfeale 17km, Tralee 26km, Limerick 77km. \r\n\r\nThe lands are located on the L10114, 3km south of the town of Listowel. Population (2022) 4,794. Listowel is a heritage market town in Co Kerry. It is on the River Feale, 28 km from the county town, Tralee. Listowel is on the N69 Limerick Foynes Tralee Road. Listowel is located at the head of the North Kerry limestone plain. Positioned in the very heart of North Kerry, its hinterland is an area of mainly dairy agricultural use. Listowel is serviced by many primary, post-primary and post-leaving certificate education facilities. There are a host of bars, restaurants, cafes, shops, and sporting clubs. Tralee is a short drive is where further amenities and transport links are to be found. \r\n\r\nDescription KY4141 PART OF \r\n\r\nThe lands are contained within folio KY4141 and amount c. 24.69ha - c. 61 acres. The subject lands are in one irregular shaped block on either side of a minor road. The subject lands are laid out in large manageable divisions, with mature boundaries of hedging and trees. The lands are all in grass of reasonable quality, suited to livestock and associated farming. Centrally located is a farmyard containing various agricultural sheds. There is good road frontage and access from two roads. \r\n\r\nIdeal location for a one-off house, subject to the necessary planning. \r\n\r\nThe lands are being sold as seen and not subject to planning.\r\n\r\nCoordinates: 52.422339, -9.467821\r\n\r\nViewing - By appointment \r\n\r\nSolicitor Iseult Cody, Beauchamps, Sir John Rogerson's quay, Dublin 2. \r\n\r\nVAT Refer to legal contracts."
